{
  "id": "follow-up-test",
  "term": "follow-up test",
  "definition": "A follow-up test is an assessment given after earlier testing, such as a pretest and posttest, to see whether the effects of an experience or learning activity are still present over time. It helps researchers compare immediate results with later outcomes.",
